message: "If you use this software in teaching, research or a publication, please cite it as below. / Se usi questo software nella didattica o in una pubblicazione, citalo così."
title: "ZYpsilon · Projection lab"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Raffaelli
    given-names: Baires
version: 1.2.2
date-released: 2026-11-23
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24405119
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
url: "https://www.zypsilon.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zypsilon-lab/zypsilon"
abstract: >-
  Free interactive 3D laboratory for studying descriptive geometry: orthogonal
  projections (Monge), axonometry, perspective, shadows and sections with a
  cutting plane, plus an Intersection Lab for the interpenetration of two
  solids by the cutting-plane method. Drawings are laid out on an A4, A3 or A2
  drawing sheet (in centimetres, 1:1) and can be downloaded as PNG or PDF.
  Interface in English, Italian and Chinese.
keywords:
  - descriptive geometry
  - orthogonal projections
  - Monge
  - axonometry
  - perspective
  - shadows
  - interpenetration of solids
  - geometry education
  - three.js
